classDiagram
    direction TB

    class DocumentEditor {
        -vector~string~ documentElements
        -string renderedDocument
        +addText(string text)
        +addImage(string imagePath)
        +renderDocument() string
        +saveToFile()
    }

    class Main {
        +main()
    }

    Main --> DocumentEditor : uses

    note for DocumentEditor "Bad Design Highlights:
1) Raw string data model (text/image both as string)
2) Runtime type detection via file extension
3) Rendering + persistence + data management in one class
4) Cached renderedDocument can become stale after new edits"

    %% Runtime decision flow (embedded as note for clarity)
    note for Main "Flow:
main() -> addText/addImage
-> renderDocument()
   loop each element
      if endsWith .jpg/.png => [Image: path]
      else => plain text
-> saveToFile() -> document.txt"
